-- statement:
--   An auxiliary lemma of the round-six development, published as a separate node because its proof is long or shared.
--
--   The following holds (Lean statement, in the scope of module `NLogN.TM`):
--
--   ```lean
--   theorem NLogN.sim_pop (c : Cfg S) (hpc : c.pc < L) (i : Fin S) (e : ℕ) (he : e < L)
--       (hcode : code c.pc = .pop i e) :
--       Reach gst (progOf code L pc0) (⟨c.pc, hpc⟩, false) (enc inp c) 1 (⟨e, he⟩, false)
--         (enc inp ⟨e, c.σ.pop i, c.ctl⟩)
--   ```
--
--   **Context.** Running flat code on the platform's Turing machines
--
--   Tapes: `0` input, `1` output, `2` control stack (return addresses), `3 + i` stack `i`.
--   On every stack tape the head rests on the top symbol (on `▷` when empty), so `push` is two
--   steps, `pop` and tests are one step, and a call is two steps.  Each flat step is at most two
--   machine steps (`flat_tm`).
